	<description>Anna is a writer, author of one very successful novel, who now keeps four notebooks. In one, with a black cover, she reviews the African experience of her earlier year. In a red one she records her political life, her disillusionment with communism. In a yellow one she writes a novel in which the heroine reviles part of her own experience. And in the blue one she keeps a personal diary. Finally, in love with an American writer and threatened with insanity, Anna tries to bring the threads of all four books together in a golden notebook.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Doris Lessing's best-known and most influential novel, &lt;i&gt;The Golden Notebook&lt;/i&gt; retains its extraordinary power and relevance decades after its initial publication.</description>
